    <h2>When a spreadsheet beats a document</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Sort and filter freely</h3>
        <p>Booked everything out of order? Sort by date and it reorganizes itself. No cutting and pasting paragraphs around like you'd have to in a document.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Running cost total built in</h3>
        <p>Each row has a cost column that feeds a running total at the top, so you can see what the trip is actually costing as you book, without a separate budget tool.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Multiple views of the same trip</h3>
        <p>Duplicate a tab to make a "by day" view and a "by category" view (all the flights together, all the meals together) from the same underlying data.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Plays well with a budget template</h3>
        <p>If you're also using our <a href="/templates/trip-budget-template/">trip budget template</a>, the cost columns are laid out the same way, so copying numbers between them is a straight paste.</p>
